ng  more snow melt from the mountains flow  into the basin which means less water  for residents and farmers  but salt lake city barely has enough  water to support long-term needs of its  population a report commissioned by  utah's legislature found that the  state's demand for water would outpace  supply by about 2040.  last december salt lake city stopped  issuing permits for businesses that  require significant water such as data  centers or bottling plants raising the  price of water could also help  conservation efforts  if you  have incentives like that to say well  we're going to increase your water bill  by you know 15  per annum in order to make sure that we  can save the lake  will people be happy with that will they  accept that in utah's recent state  legislative session lawmakers approved a  range of projects to protect the  long-term health of the great salt lake  this past legislative session was a  tremendous win for great salt lake and  we had over  500 million dollars in projects that  will be directly impacting great salt  lake and we're optimistic that those  will help us bring water to the lake  [Music]
 

